'''Bannari Amman Group''' is an [[Conglomerate (company)|industrial conglomerate]] based in [[Tamil Nadu]], with presence in [[manufacturing]], [[trading]] and service.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://economictimes.indiatimes.com/bannari-amman-sugars-ltd/infocompanyhistory/companyid-13995.cms|title=Bannari Amman Sugars Ltd. (stock brief and company history)|date=12 August 2011|work=The Economic Times|publisher=Times Internet Ltd.|accessdate=14 August 2011}}</ref> Manufacturing and trading activities include [[sugar]], [[ethanol|alcohol]], [[liquor]], [[granite]] etc.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.scholarshipsinindia.com/courses/bannari_amman_institute_of_technology.html|title=Bannari Amman Institute of Technology|work=ScholarshipsinIndia.com|accessdate=14 August 2011}}</ref> The service sector has [[wind power]] energy, [[education]] etc. It was founded by S. V. Balasubramaniam who is the Chairman of the group.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.hindu.com/2008/03/30/stories/2008033056191200.htm|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080402224918/http://www.hindu.com/2008/03/30/stories/2008033056191200.htm|url-status=dead|archive-date=2 April 2008|title=Bannari Amman group, Brandot Intl. form venture|last=Staff reporter|date=30 March 2008|work=[[The Hindu]]|accessdate=14 August 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.hindu.com/2011/06/08/stories/2011060855820200.htm|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110611050547/http://www.hindu.com/2011/06/08/stories/2011060855820200.htm|url-status=dead|archive-date=11 June 2011|title=Festo centre for automation at Bannari to make students fit for industry|last=Staff reporter|date=8 June 2011|work=[[The Hindu]]|accessdate=14 August 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Coimbatore/article531666.ece|title=Government appreciation for Bannari group|last=Staff reporter|date=24 July 2010|work=The Hindu|accessdate=14 August 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.hindu.com/2009/12/11/stories/2009121156900100.htm|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091215224200/http://www.hindu.com/2009/12/11/stories/2009121156900100.htm|url-status=dead|archive-date=15 December 2009|title=Bannari Rural Foundation helps govt school students get better education|last=Madhavan|first=Karthik|date=11 December 2009|work=[[The Hindu]]|accessdate=14 August 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://in.reuters.com/article/idINIndia-34260220080627|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160306173136/http://in.reuters.com/article/idINIndia-34260220080627|url-status=dead|archive-date=6 March 2016|title=Rates, inflation bitters spoil sugarmakers party|last=Pandley|first=Swati|date=27 June 2008|work=Reuters India|publisher=Thomson Reuters|accessdate=14 August 2011|location=Mumbai, India}}</ref>

== History ==
In the beginning 1980s, BAG mainly was a sugar manufacturer.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.bannari.com/sugar.html|title=Bannari Sugar}}</ref> The by-product of the sugar production - [[Molasses]] - was used for their distilleries.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://biospectrumindia.ciol.com/content/BioBusiness/10705074.asp |title=Bannari Amman Group starts Tamil Nadu's first biodiesel plant |last=Suresh |first=N |date=7 June 2007 |work=BioSpectrumIndia |publisher=Cybermedia |accessdate=14 August 2011 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20111003124227/http://biospectrumindia.ciol.com/content/BioBusiness/10705074.asp |archivedate=3 October 2011 }}</ref>

